                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.9414/8: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Second Secretary of Legation in China</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Atcheson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-06-28T10:00:00+08:00">June 28, 1935—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received June 28—4:58 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>185. My 177, June 22, 10 a.m. Ministers of Industries and Navy confirm remarks of
                    officials previously mentioned. Both state Pratas Reef is of no real value and
                    could not be used for naval or aviation station. According to the latter the sea
                    frequently washes over it and while the Chinese Navy maintains a weather report
                    broadcasting station there a former lighthouse has been abandoned.</p>
                <p>To the Department and Legation.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Atcheson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
